WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.890
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:25.160 --> 00:29.410
[Live Forever]

3
00:30.490 --> 00:32.940
[Episode 2]

4
00:33.980 --> 00:35.970
[2026]

5
00:35.270 --> 00:36.470
For ordinary people,

6
00:37.200 --> 00:38.920
marriage may be

7
00:39.150 --> 00:40.150
the most sincere and intimate relationship

8
00:40.150 --> 00:42.840
they will ever have.

9
00:43.970 --> 00:44.940
Loyalty

10
00:45.860 --> 00:47.090
is the promise of exclusivity

11
00:47.090 --> 00:49.090
that binds two people in a marriage.

12
00:50.900 --> 00:52.970
But for some people,

13
00:53.410 --> 00:56.460
marriage is just a seasoning for a long life,

14
00:57.500 --> 00:58.730
or

15
00:59.290 --> 01:01.420
a badge they wear in a game.

16
01:09.120 --> 01:10.380
Honey.

17
01:10.539 --> 01:13.420
Can you cut it a little smaller next time?

18
01:13.500 --> 01:15.420
I can't even chew it.

19
01:15.990 --> 01:16.789
No problem.

20
01:23.480 --> 01:25.910
You came out to see me wearing a ring.

21
01:26.360 --> 01:27.890
Aren't you afraid she'll find out?

22
01:27.890 --> 01:28.810
What's there to be afraid of?

23
01:28.810 --> 01:30.860
Afraid she'll be jealous.

24
01:33.229 --> 01:34.390
Then

25
01:35.090 --> 01:35.979
wouldn't this

26
01:37.060 --> 01:38.860
just make her even more jealous?

27
01:42.039 --> 01:43.479
You're such a tease.

28
01:45.220 --> 01:48.620
Then if she and I fell into the water together,

29
01:49.140 --> 01:50.539
who would you save first?

30
01:50.810 --> 01:54.340
That sounds like a classic wife-and-mother-in-law question.

31
01:57.090 --> 01:58.530
Of course I'd save you.

32
02:00.980 --> 02:02.730
She won't die anyway.

33
02:06.060 --> 02:07.060
How does it taste?

34
02:07.360 --> 02:09.220
I prepared it especially for you.

35
02:13.760 --> 02:15.220
It's from the Alba region.

36
02:16.530 --> 02:18.079
But there was too much rain this year,

37
02:18.079 --> 02:20.940
so the aroma is a bit lighter than in previous years.

38
02:21.650 --> 02:22.940
It's handled okay.

39
02:23.360 --> 02:24.890
The finish lingers longer.

40
02:26.020 --> 02:26.850
Miss Song,

41
02:27.340 --> 02:28.900
these are my family heirlooms.

42
02:28.900 --> 02:30.090
Pick whatever

43
02:30.090 --> 02:31.090
you like.

44
02:31.370 --> 02:33.770
You don't need to consider the price at all.

45
02:46.690 --> 02:48.020
To be honest,

46
02:48.570 --> 02:50.570
they are all tacky.

47
02:52.470 --> 02:54.740
Where is the auction invitation you promised me?

48
02:54.740 --> 02:55.670
What do you mean?

49
02:55.880 --> 02:57.280
It's right here.

50
02:59.130 --> 03:00.410
He's no good.

51
03:00.590 --> 03:01.740
I'm in a hurry to meet someone else.

52
03:01.740 --> 03:03.670
I won't be home for dinner tonight.

53
03:05.940 --> 03:07.540
See you next time, Miss Lin.

54
03:10.160 --> 03:11.240
Ning Changyue,

55
03:11.780 --> 03:12.940
why is she here?

56
03:13.810 --> 03:16.010
Is it fun to bring your ex-wife on a date?

57
03:16.850 --> 03:17.620
Wait,

58
03:18.620 --> 03:20.500
you two still live together?

59
03:21.829 --> 03:23.360
I've already paid the bill.

60
03:23.810 --> 03:24.690
Ning Changyue.

61
03:25.310 --> 03:25.940
Love you, baby.

62
03:25.940 --> 03:26.850
Ning Changyue!

63
03:31.500 --> 03:32.130
Wait!

64
03:34.670 --> 03:35.470
Give me a ride.

65
03:35.780 --> 03:36.620
Sure.

66
03:38.390 --> 03:39.270
Miss Lin.

67
03:45.320 --> 03:45.920
Miss Song.

68
03:48.300 --> 03:48.850
Hey.

69
03:49.170 --> 03:50.450
Why did I see Miss Song go over there?

70
03:50.450 --> 03:51.650
Call her Auntie Song.

71
03:52.700 --> 03:55.760
You didn't get caught by her while out on a date, did you?

72
03:56.550 --> 03:57.329
What do you mean?

73
03:57.329 --> 03:58.860
Isn't she here on a date too?

74
03:59.090 --> 04:00.180
For young people,

75
04:00.320 --> 04:02.280
this is a healthy relationship.

76
04:02.790 --> 04:06.550
[Healthy Relationship]

77
04:03.900 --> 04:06.300
A healthy relationship?

78
04:10.840 --> 04:11.810
[2000]

79
04:12.530 --> 04:13.500
Song Yiqiu,

80
04:13.740 --> 04:14.900
let's

81
04:15.940 --> 04:17.000
be together again.

82
04:17.450 --> 04:19.370
We began this journey to immortality together,

83
04:19.370 --> 04:19.860
so let's

84
04:21.250 --> 04:22.780
bring it to an end together.

85
04:29.700 --> 04:30.730
Really nice.

86
04:30.770 --> 04:32.010
Italian decoration.

87
04:32.440 --> 04:33.180
Very good.

88
04:34.180 --> 04:35.540
Put that Ming Dynasty vase

89
04:35.540 --> 04:37.010
on the third shelf of the display cabinet.

90
04:37.010 --> 04:38.930
The painting is crooked. A little to the left.

91
04:38.930 --> 04:39.520
Forget it.

92
04:39.520 --> 04:40.520
I'll do it myself.

93
04:40.770 --> 04:41.690
Ning Changyue.

94
04:42.250 --> 04:43.570
You can move in,

95
04:43.810 --> 04:45.690
but we need to set some ground rules.

96
04:45.690 --> 04:46.540
First,

97
04:47.060 --> 04:48.620
don't touch my things.

98
04:48.930 --> 04:49.860
Second,

99
04:50.130 --> 04:51.210
when I'm not talking to you,

100
04:51.210 --> 04:52.450
don't talk to me.

101
04:52.480 --> 04:53.400
Third,

102
04:53.480 --> 04:54.800
if I'm upset,

103
04:54.890 --> 04:56.860
don't show up in front of me.

104
04:57.950 --> 04:59.340
The first two are fine.

105
04:59.370 --> 05:00.370
As for the third,

106
05:00.400 --> 05:02.800
how am I supposed to know when you're upset?

107
05:02.960 --> 05:05.290
This Ming Dynasty piece is still the best.

108
05:07.330 --> 05:09.060
So you mean

109
05:09.970 --> 05:11.460
you disagree?

110
05:12.850 --> 05:13.510
Be careful!

111
05:15.500 --> 05:16.560
What are you doing?

112
05:16.620 --> 05:18.620
After all, if these

113
05:18.890 --> 05:20.420
Ming Dynasty vases break,

114
05:20.420 --> 05:22.060
they're just shards of pottery.

115
05:22.060 --> 05:22.580
Okay, okay.

116
05:22.580 --> 05:23.510
Whatever you say.

117
05:23.510 --> 05:24.240
Give it to me.

118
05:33.010 --> 05:34.320
My stocks.

119
05:34.900 --> 05:37.340
My stocks, my stocks.

120
05:37.940 --> 05:39.860
The weather is so nice today.

121
05:39.860 --> 05:43.250
We must have a perfect Christmas.

122
05:52.860 --> 05:54.450
Ning Changyue.

123
05:58.480 --> 05:59.460
What's wrong?

124
05:59.659 --> 06:01.060
My little Qiuqiu.

125
06:04.410 --> 06:06.170
Merry Christmas.

126
06:21.100 --> 06:22.100
Wait a minute.

127
06:22.210 --> 06:23.130
Are you selling it or not?

128
06:23.130 --> 06:24.100
Let me think about it.

129
06:24.100 --> 06:26.210
Why are you so indecisive?

130
06:26.300 --> 06:27.130
What do you know?

131
06:27.130 --> 06:28.010
This is the first edition.

132
06:28.010 --> 06:29.500
Song Yiqiu, be the judge.

133
06:33.950 --> 06:35.550
You little brat.

134
06:36.440 --> 06:37.390
Take it away.

135
06:41.500 --> 06:43.170
Much quieter now.

136
06:46.320 --> 06:47.520
No, I don't want it.

137
06:50.320 --> 06:55.380
[2026]

138
06:55.890 --> 06:57.690
I've known you for so many years.

139
06:58.570 --> 07:00.370
When have you ever been healthy?

140
07:09.330 --> 07:10.450
Handle with care.

141
07:10.660 --> 07:11.980
That's Ming Dynasty rosewood.

142
07:11.980 --> 07:12.980
If it breaks,

143
07:13.100 --> 07:15.430
even selling you wouldn't cover the cost.

144
07:15.940 --> 07:17.540
These treasures of yours

145
07:17.540 --> 07:19.180
are worth more than me.

146
07:20.810 --> 07:22.810
Take your time.

147
07:22.810 --> 07:23.740
Enjoy your meal.

148
07:24.100 --> 07:25.420
I'm off work!

149
07:27.010 --> 07:29.660
You have quite the style now.

150
07:29.850 --> 07:31.110
It's the 21st century,

151
07:31.130 --> 07:32.930
and you still have an entourage.

152
07:33.010 --> 07:34.300
They're called employees now,

153
07:34.300 --> 07:35.300
old lady.

154
07:36.060 --> 07:37.180
We offer full social insurance and housing provident fund benefits,

155
07:37.180 --> 07:39.300
legal employment, and a formal employment contract.

156
07:39.300 --> 07:40.250
You've been living

157
07:40.250 --> 07:42.580
too comfortably these past twenty years.

158
07:42.980 --> 07:45.610
Drinking tea, appraising antiques, and ordering people around.

159
07:45.610 --> 07:46.930
Have you forgotten

160
07:46.980 --> 07:49.100
why we've been pretending to live in harmony

161
07:49.100 --> 07:50.060
under this roof?

162
07:50.060 --> 07:51.790
Of course I haven't forgotten.

163
07:52.159 --> 07:53.480
I'm not like some people

164
07:53.480 --> 07:55.210
who use blind dates as an excuse

165
07:55.450 --> 07:56.330
to trick those

166
07:56.330 --> 07:58.180
rich and resourceful collectors

167
07:58.180 --> 07:59.480
into finding the osmanthus tree.

168
07:59.480 --> 08:01.500
I'll give her credit for coming up with that one.

169
08:01.500 --> 08:03.660
At least I'm genuinely trying to find it.

170
08:03.660 --> 08:04.570
What about you?

171
08:04.600 --> 08:06.790
Miss Lin, Miss Wang and Miss Liu.

172
08:07.130 --> 08:08.980
Are you looking for a painting

173
08:09.130 --> 08:10.360
or holding a beauty pageant?

174
08:10.360 --> 08:12.000
At least I'm efficient.

175
08:12.240 --> 08:13.260
Unlike some people

176
08:13.260 --> 08:14.620
who've been going on blind dates for ages

177
08:14.620 --> 08:17.500
and still end up with nothing but vulgar types.

178
08:17.740 --> 08:19.980
Even a vulgar type

179
08:21.420 --> 08:22.860
is better than you.

180
08:23.010 --> 08:24.210
Deceiving a young girl's feelings

181
08:24.210 --> 08:25.180
to get information.

182
08:25.180 --> 08:27.060
Where's your conscience, Commander Ning?

183
08:27.060 --> 08:27.980
Conscience?

184
08:27.980 --> 08:28.620
My lady.

185
08:28.620 --> 08:29.740
Did you think about morality

186
08:29.740 --> 08:31.400
when you threw the knife at me?

187
08:49.020 --> 08:49.730
Song Yiqiu.

188
08:49.970 --> 08:50.610
You owe me!

189
08:50.730 --> 08:52.940
You've lived in my house for over 20 years,

190
08:52.940 --> 08:54.420
and I fed you well.

191
08:54.420 --> 08:55.500
Have you ever paid rent?

192
08:55.500 --> 08:56.530
20 years?

193
08:56.940 --> 08:57.940
In these 20 years,

194
08:57.940 --> 08:59.180
the treasures of mine you broke

195
08:59.180 --> 09:00.660
could buy 20 of your crappy houses.

196
09:00.660 --> 09:01.730
Crappy house?

197
09:02.020 --> 09:03.330
Then move out!

198
09:03.330 --> 09:05.540
After all, we both lived just fine

199
09:05.540 --> 09:06.660
for those 72 years without each other.

200
09:06.660 --> 09:07.570
72 years?

201
09:07.570 --> 09:09.330
It's 72 years and 37 days.

202
09:09.330 --> 09:10.450
You have such a good memory.

203
09:10.450 --> 09:11.940
Do you need me to praise you?

204
09:11.940 --> 09:13.180
Move out.

205
09:13.180 --> 09:15.610
I want you to move out right now!

206
09:15.610 --> 09:16.300
Fine.

207
09:16.300 --> 09:17.330
You know what?

208
09:17.330 --> 09:18.660
Property prices have dropped.

209
09:18.660 --> 09:20.690
I'll go buy a bigger house than yours.

210
09:20.690 --> 09:21.780
Ning Changyue.

211
09:22.180 --> 09:23.570
Move out.

212
09:23.570 --> 09:24.420
Breaking news.

213
09:24.420 --> 09:26.610
A man has reportedly been turned into an osmanthus sapling

214
09:26.610 --> 09:28.490
and buried in Chengxi Park.

215
09:28.900 --> 09:30.180
According to witnesses,

216
09:30.180 --> 09:32.690
there was another young woman at the scene.

217
09:32.970 --> 09:35.110
She is believed to be around 18 years old.

218
09:35.110 --> 09:36.420
Her identity is unknown,

219
09:36.420 --> 09:40.420
and she is currently being held at the Chengxi Neighborhood Committee.

220
09:43.300 --> 09:45.300
-Osmanthus tree. -Osmanthus tree.

221
10:03.780 --> 10:05.910
-Excuse me. -I'm here to find my child.

222
10:07.970 --> 10:08.690
What's going on?

223
10:08.690 --> 10:10.810
Ma'am.

224
10:12.540 --> 10:14.330
We lost our child.

225
10:14.330 --> 10:15.730
Calm down, calm down.

226
10:15.730 --> 10:17.660
Take your time, I'll register it.

227
10:17.660 --> 10:19.460
Come, let's get you registered.

228
10:23.660 --> 10:25.020
Sit down, honey.

229
10:28.490 --> 10:30.260
Tell me what happened.

230
10:30.590 --> 10:31.870
Our child...

231
10:31.900 --> 10:34.260
Our child is lost.

232
10:34.690 --> 10:35.380
I saw...

233
10:35.380 --> 10:37.210
I saw it on TV.

234
10:37.210 --> 10:38.660
Look at her photo.

235
10:38.810 --> 10:40.090
She's very pretty.

236
10:40.090 --> 10:40.940
Yes.

237
10:40.940 --> 10:41.540
Look.

238
10:41.780 --> 10:42.850
Let me see.

239
10:42.850 --> 10:44.260
Take a look.

240
10:48.000 --> 10:49.720
Honey, don't cry.

241
10:49.750 --> 10:52.040
You won't cry once we find her.

242
10:52.140 --> 10:53.690
You look so pretty even when you cry.

243
10:53.690 --> 10:54.260
Come.

244
10:54.260 --> 10:55.140
Have some tea.

245
10:55.140 --> 10:56.090
No.

246
10:56.090 --> 10:57.380
I want my girl.

247
10:57.540 --> 10:58.490
I want my girl.

248
10:58.490 --> 11:00.900
Say something.

249
11:01.330 --> 11:02.300
Okay, okay.

250
11:02.300 --> 11:03.300
My wife hasn't

251
11:03.300 --> 11:04.540
slept well for days.

252
11:04.540 --> 11:05.180
Sorry to bother you.

253
11:05.180 --> 11:06.840
We'll take our child home now.

254
11:08.330 --> 11:09.660
Yours?

255
11:10.690 --> 11:12.050
Biological?

256
11:14.850 --> 11:15.940
That's not right.

257
11:16.060 --> 11:18.540
You two are just in your early thirties.

258
11:19.500 --> 11:21.430
And this girl is already 18.

259
11:21.660 --> 11:23.180
We got married early.

260
11:23.180 --> 11:24.850
And we take good care of ourselves.

261
11:24.850 --> 11:27.050
Did you bring your household register?

262
11:33.250 --> 11:34.650
I don't know the process.

263
11:37.490 --> 11:38.570
I knew it.

264
11:39.060 --> 11:41.060
There's something wrong with you two.

265
11:41.060 --> 11:42.020
I'm calling the...

266
11:42.020 --> 11:43.180
Time, freeze!

267
12:06.300 --> 12:07.810
Princess and Guard.

268
12:08.300 --> 12:10.210
Are you here to take me home?

269
12:35.020 --> 12:36.870
Back in the Southern Qin,

270
12:37.180 --> 12:39.580
your hand was chained to that iron chain.

271
12:40.020 --> 12:42.020
That was when you gave us the elixir.

272
12:48.300 --> 12:49.490
Eat it.

273
12:52.180 --> 12:55.140
Maybe you can get a chance to be together forever.

274
13:07.980 --> 13:09.310
You forgot everything?

275
13:11.570 --> 13:13.120
What's wrong with the princess?

276
13:13.120 --> 13:15.380
Is there something wrong with her brain?

277
13:16.860 --> 13:17.420
I've asked everything

278
13:17.420 --> 13:18.340
you wanted to ask.

279
13:18.340 --> 13:19.320
What she remembers

280
13:19.320 --> 13:20.980
depends entirely on her mood.

281
13:21.490 --> 13:22.420
It's choking me.

282
13:22.940 --> 13:23.490
Watch closely.

283
13:23.490 --> 13:26.000
Nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium in a 1:1:1 ratio.

284
13:26.000 --> 13:27.060
Don't move around,

285
13:27.690 --> 13:29.420
or it won't be absorbed evenly.

286
13:33.060 --> 13:36.660
Your skills are much better than in the Republic of China era.

287
13:37.380 --> 13:38.510
You still remember.

288
13:38.690 --> 13:39.730
Thank you.

289
13:39.760 --> 13:41.620
You make a fuss every few decades.

290
13:41.660 --> 13:42.810
This time you even got on TV.

291
13:42.810 --> 13:44.540
How am I the one making a fuss?

292
13:44.850 --> 13:46.540
He provoked me.

293
13:47.610 --> 13:50.690
Why are you littering?

294
13:50.970 --> 13:53.780
Pick up this trash by the tree right now.

295
13:53.850 --> 13:55.060
I'll only say it once.

296
13:57.330 --> 13:58.540
Apologize to them.

297
14:00.420 --> 14:02.280
Are sanitation workers nowadays

298
14:02.320 --> 14:04.670
all this good-looking?

299
14:04.690 --> 14:06.770
You've used up your chance.

300
14:32.940 --> 14:34.980
She gave us eternal life,

301
14:35.010 --> 14:37.290
but she completely forgot about it herself.

302
14:37.290 --> 14:39.450
She's much better than in the Republic of China era.

303
14:39.450 --> 14:41.380
Now she even knows how to talk back.

304
14:44.850 --> 14:46.730
So you're telling me

305
14:47.300 --> 14:49.250
I'm supposed to keep taking care of her,

306
14:49.250 --> 14:51.850
wait until she gets her memories back someday,

307
14:51.900 --> 14:54.780
and then ask her how to end this immortality?

308
14:57.180 --> 14:59.540
Have you seen what you two have done

309
14:59.540 --> 15:01.470
to my garden?

310
15:01.500 --> 15:03.580
You've trashed this beautiful garden,

311
15:03.580 --> 15:05.980
and you expect me to keep taking care of her?

312
15:16.540 --> 15:19.420
Anyway, until we put an end to this immortality for good,

313
15:19.420 --> 15:21.810
I think the three of us should live together.

314
15:21.810 --> 15:23.020
What three?

315
15:23.050 --> 15:24.520
It's just me.

316
15:24.980 --> 15:27.780
Did you forget you were just kicked out yesterday?

317
15:28.230 --> 15:29.030
Come on.

318
15:32.870 --> 15:34.130
Think about it carefully.

319
15:34.130 --> 15:36.320
This is our only clue in 26 years.

320
15:36.900 --> 15:39.570
This clue is now planted in that flowerpot.

321
15:54.330 --> 15:56.300
Then clean all this up.

322
15:56.300 --> 15:58.300
It's all piled up in a mess.

323
15:58.330 --> 15:59.930
If I catch you doing it again,

324
16:00.400 --> 16:02.060
you'll live in the garden too.

325
16:07.940 --> 16:10.660
Why does the princess seem like a different person?

326
16:10.660 --> 16:12.620
She's not quite the same as before.

327
16:13.090 --> 16:14.400
Why did I also hear

328
16:14.510 --> 16:17.240
that you are looking for a way to end eternal life?

329
16:18.260 --> 16:19.180
Yes.

330
16:19.690 --> 16:20.330
Why?

331
16:20.620 --> 16:22.350
Didn't you want to live before?

332
16:25.450 --> 16:26.850
Maybe we forgot

333
16:28.170 --> 16:29.520
why we wanted to live.

334
16:31.210 --> 16:32.210
I'm done talking.

335
16:39.490 --> 16:41.090
What did you drop?

336
16:43.850 --> 16:44.640
This.

337
16:48.140 --> 16:50.080
It has an ancient smell.

338
16:56.260 --> 16:57.970
What did you feel?

339
17:08.950 --> 17:10.230
I'm thirsty.

340
17:10.250 --> 17:10.800
Okay.

341
17:10.829 --> 17:11.589
Coming.

342
17:15.619 --> 17:16.690
That painting just now,

343
17:16.690 --> 17:18.150
Autumn Moon in the Forest,

344
17:18.170 --> 17:20.490
seems to be a sacred painting of the Osmanthus Clan.

345
17:20.490 --> 17:21.250
Could it be connected to

346
17:21.250 --> 17:22.970
our Live Forever Contract?

347
17:24.450 --> 17:25.730
Next up

348
17:25.510 --> 17:27.349
[Yide Auction Co., Ltd.]

349
17:26.490 --> 17:28.099
is Autumn Moon in the Forest.

350
17:30.660 --> 17:32.530
The artist and exact date

351
17:32.530 --> 17:33.890
of this painting are unknown.

352
17:33.890 --> 17:35.450
However, experts have determined that

353
17:35.450 --> 17:37.970
it dates back at least two thousand years.

354
17:38.080 --> 17:41.770
Its depiction of mountains and rivers, along with its distinctive brushwork,

355
17:41.770 --> 17:43.490
is exceptionally rare for its time.

356
17:43.490 --> 17:45.960
It is also being shown to the public for the first time.

357
17:45.960 --> 17:47.850
At the collector's request,

358
17:48.130 --> 17:50.650
the painting cannot be fully unveiled at this time.

359
17:50.650 --> 17:52.210
We appreciate your understanding.

360
17:52.210 --> 17:54.010
The opening bid is 800,000 yuan.

361
17:54.380 --> 17:55.510
Bidding starts now.

362
17:59.940 --> 18:02.050
A piece by an unknown artist

363
18:02.050 --> 18:03.620
with no known provenance,

364
18:03.620 --> 18:05.680
yet they dare to sell it half-hidden.

365
18:05.850 --> 18:07.160
Who would buy it?

366
18:07.420 --> 18:07.860
Uncle,

367
18:08.210 --> 18:10.490
are we going to bid on this painting?

368
18:11.340 --> 18:13.210
I don't think it's worth that much.

369
18:13.210 --> 18:14.250
Let them bid.

370
18:14.250 --> 18:15.210
I'm not bidding.

371
18:15.240 --> 18:17.370
This painting is actually quite good.

372
18:17.860 --> 18:21.340
It contains the time of those bound by the pact.

373
18:21.620 --> 18:22.900
As long as you get it

374
18:22.940 --> 18:25.200
and release your time from the painting,

375
18:25.210 --> 18:26.870
you can end your immortality.

376
18:27.310 --> 18:30.660
But are you sure you want to do this?

377
18:33.250 --> 18:34.050
Let's go.

378
18:34.820 --> 18:36.880
Are we really just leaving like this?

379
19:16.100 --> 19:18.970
Mr. 250, one million, going once.
